      </div>
      <div class="space-y-4">{[{q:"What is intelligent document processing?",a:"Intelligent document processing (IDP) is a technology that uses AI, machine learning, and OCR to automatically extract, classify, and process data from documents like invoices, receipts, forms, and reports. Unlike basic OCR which only converts images to text, IDP understands document structure, identifies relationships between data fields, and organizes information into usable formats like Excel or CSV. DocDataEntry is an intelligent document processing platform that adds transparent confidence scoring to every field it extracts."},{q:"What is a word processing document?",a:"A word processing document is a file created with word processing software such as Microsoft Word, Google Docs, or LibreOffice. Common formats include DOCX, DOC, and RTF. These documents contain formatted text, images, tables, and other elements. DocDataEntry can extract data from word processing documents along with PDFs and images, making it a versatile document processing tool for any business."},{q:"What are document processes?",a:"Document processes refer to the workflows involved in handling documents from receipt to final storage. This includes capturing (scanning or uploading), classifying (identifying document type), extracting (pulling out key data fields), validating (checking accuracy), and exporting (saving in the desired format). DocDataEntry automates all these steps with AI, reducing manual data entry time by up to 80%. The confidence scoring system validates extracted data automatically."},{q:"What is document analyzer AI?",a:"A document analyzer AI is an artificial intelligence system that reads, understands, and extracts data from documents automatically. It uses computer vision to see document layouts, natural language processing to understand text, and machine learning to improve accuracy over time. DocDataEntry's document analyzer AI processes invoices, receipts, forms, and reports, assigning a confidence score to every field it extracts so you know exactly which data to trust."},{q:"How does free AI document analysis work?",a:"Free AI document analysis works by uploading your document to an AI-powered platform that processes it at no cost. DocDataEntry offers a free tier that processes up to 10 documents per month with full confidence scoring. Simply upload your PDF, image, or Word document, and the AI automatically detects tables, form fields, headers, and data. Each extracted field gets a confidence score from 0-100%, and fields below 90% are flagged for your review."},{q:"Where can I use a document analyzer online free?",a:"You can use DocDataEntry's document analyzer online free right here on this website. No sign-up required for the free tier. Simply go to the Upload page, select your document (PDF, image, or DOCX), and the AI will extract structured data with confidence scores. Results can be exported to Excel, CSV, or JSON. It's the most transparent free AI document analysis tool available."},{q:"How does AI document processing save time for accountants?",a:"Accountants spend hours manually entering data from client invoices and receipts into accounting software. DocDataEntry's AI document processing extracts all key fields automatically: invoice numbers, dates, vendor names, amounts, tax, and line items. The confidence scoring means you only review fields the AI is unsure about (typically 10-20%), cutting review time by 80%. This frees accountants to focus on advisory work instead of data entry."},{q:"Is intelligent document processing secure?",a:"Yes. DocDataEntry uses industry-standard security including encryption in transit (TLS 1.3) and at rest (AES-256). Your documents are processed in isolated secure environments and automatically deleted within 24 hours. Extracted data is never shared with third parties. We comply with SOC 2 and GDPR standards for data protection."},{q:"What types of documents can be processed?",a:"DocDataEntry processes a wide range of business documents: invoices, receipts, purchase orders, bank statements, insurance forms, contracts, resumes/CVs, medical forms, tax documents, shipping labels, and table-heavy reports. We support PDF, PNG, JPG, and DOCX input formats with output to Excel (XLSX), CSV, JSON, and XML."}].map(function(faq){return'<div class="faq-item rounded-2xl border border-neutral-800 bg-neutral-900/30 transition-all hover:border-neutral-700"><button class="faq-question flex w-full items-center justify-between px-6 py-5 text-left"><span class="text-base font-medium text-neutral-200">'+faq.q+'</span><svg class="faq-icon h-5 w-5 shrink-0 text-neutral-500 transition-transform duration-300" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M19 9l-7 7-7-7"/></svg></button><div class="faq-answer hidden px-6 pb-5"><p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-neutral-400">'+faq.a+'</p></div></div>'}).join('')}</div>
